1.2 Architecture Flow
The client (React frontend) sends HTTP requests to the Spring Boot REST API. The API
layer authenticates the request via JWT, applies business logic, and communicates with the
PostgreSQL database using JPA repositories. Responses are returned as JSON payloads to
the frontend.
Frontend (React + Tailwind) → REST API (Spring Boot) → JPA / Hibernate →
PostgreSQL (Supabase)
