6. Security and Performance Considerations
6.1 Security
•
•
•
•
•
•
All passwords stored as BCrypt hashes — raw passwords never persisted.
JWT tokens include expiry (15 min access / 7 day refresh) to limit exposure.
Spring Security enforces role-based access: USER vs ADMIN routes are strictly
separated.
Razorpay webhook signature is verified using HMAC-SHA256 before updating order
status.
Input validation via Spring's @Valid and Bean Validation annotations prevents
injection attacks.
HTTPS enforced on all production endpoints via Railway and Vercel configurations.
6.2 Performance
•
•
•
•
HikariCP connection pooling minimizes database connection overhead.
Pagination implemented on all list endpoints to avoid large data payloads.
React lazy loading and code splitting for faster frontend load times.
Database indexes on frequently queried columns: email, category_id, product name.
